       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Ordered:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Usual limits:** a single dose is typically capped at 800 mg. The maximum daily dose is 3,200 mg for adults under physician supervision. This order is twice the daily maximum, and each dose is twice the usual single-dose maximum.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove those risks.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nPlease tell me which of these you intended. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, confirm that and give a rationale. I'll then enter it with a note, though I'd recommend pharmacy review first."
