       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day is double the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen. I don't know of any indication where that dose is appropriate. Higher doses add no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, and they sharply raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, renal injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **A lower dose** that fits the indication, such as 400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours.\n\nIf you have a specific reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a research setting, please contact pharmacy or the clinical decision support team. They can review it and enter it through a channel with the right safeguards.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
